   'What is the main purpose of the Environmental Impact Statement (EIS) System in the context of sustainable development in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To expedite the approval of development projects"},{"id":"b","text":"To reduce the cost of project implementation"},{"id":"c","text":"To eliminate the need for environmental compliance certificates (ECC)"},{"id":"d","text":"To assess the potential environmental impacts of proposed projects"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g01045', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'In the framework of sustainable development, how does the establishment of buffer zones around protected areas contribute to environmental conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By allowing unrestricted resource extraction in these zones"},{"id":"b","text":"By creating spaces for intensive agriculture"},{"id":"c","text":"By enabling urban development near sensitive ecosystems"},{"id":"d","text":"By reducing human-wildlife conflict and preserving biodiversity"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g01046', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'Which of the following actions is an example of sustainable development in forestry that includes both conservation and community participation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Establishing large monoculture plantations managed by private corporations"},{"id":"b","text":"Promoting exclusive logging rights to international companies"},{"id":"c","text":"Implementing community-based forest management agreements (CBFMA)"},{"id":"d","text":"Converting forest lands into industrial zones"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g01047', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Under Philippine environmental law, which of the following is a key difference between the Community-Based Forest Management Agreement (CBFMA) and the Integrated Forest Management Agreement (IFMA) in terms of sustainable development goals?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"CBFMA allows logging without restrictions, whereas IFMA imposes strict logging bans."},{"id":"b","text":"IFMA encourages monoculture plantations, whereas CBFMA focuses on biodiversity conservation."},{"id":"c","text":"CBFMA focuses on community participation while IFMA prioritizes large-scale commercial forestry."},{"id":"d","text":"CBFMA is exclusive to government-managed lands, while IFMA applies to private lands."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g01048', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which principle of sustainable development is challenged when excessive logging in a watershed area reduces its capacity to provide clean water to downstream communities?',
