  ('fg-g01055', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'How does the principle of ''intergenerational equity'' influence sustainable forest management practices in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It mandates immediate economic gains from forest resources."},{"id":"b","text":"It focuses solely on the current population''s needs without future considerations."},{"id":"c","text":"It decreases the emphasis on conserving biodiversity."},{"id":"d","text":"It ensures that current forest use does not compromise future generations'' needs."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g01056', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the realm of sustainable forest management, which of the following practices aligns with the concept of maintaining ecosystem integrity?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clear-cutting large forest areas for timber production"},{"id":"b","text":"Promoting mixed-species plantations to mimic natural forests"},{"id":"c","text":"Converting forest lands into monoculture agricultural fields"},{"id":"d","text":"Exclusively harvesting non-timber forest products"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g01057', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Under RA 7586, also known as the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS) Act, which of the following elements is crucial for ensuring the sustainable development of a protected area while supporting biodiversity conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Expansion of agricultural lands within the protected area."},{"id":"b","text":"Zoning and buffer zone establishment within the protected area."},{"id":"c","text":"Unrestricted access for logging activities."},{"id":"d","text":"Conversion of protected areas into commercial zones."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g01058', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which of the following represents a challenge in implementing sustainable development within the framework of RA 8371, the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act, specifically in relation to forest management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensuring free and prior informed consent for development projects."},{"id":"b","text":"Replacing traditional cultural practices with modern forestry techniques."},{"id":"c","text":"Encouraging large-scale mining operations on ancestral lands."},{"id":"d","text":"Promoting monoculture plantations in indigenous territories."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g01059', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the context of the National Greening Program (NGP), which of the following is a significant challenge in aligning the program with long-term sustainable development goals?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Complete reliance on exotic tree species for reforestation."},{"id":"b","text":"Immediate economic returns from fast-growing species."},{"id":"c","text":"Minimizing community involvement in planting activities."},{"id":"d","text":"Monitoring and evaluation of tree survival rates post-planting."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g01060', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'How does the integration of Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) schemes contribute to sustainable forest management in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By promoting deforestation to maximize economic benefits."},{"id":"b","text":"By incentivizing conservation efforts and providing financial rewards for ecosystem services."},{"id":"c","text":"By reducing the need for local community participation in forest management."},{"id":"d","text":"By focusing solely on timber production for economic gain."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
